ube.com/embed/5H-ZC7VaKgk"&#10; style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;border:0;"&#10; allowfullscreen&#10; loading="lazy"&gt;&#10; &lt;/iframe&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;</description></item><item><title>404</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/404/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/404/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Experience</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/experience/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/experience/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://cv.ryancranie.com" target="_blank" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.3);"&gt;view my complete cv ↗&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="work-experience"&gt;Work Experience&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="it-workplace-support-analyst"&gt;IT Workplace Support Analyst&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="sefe-energy--august-2025--present"&gt;SEFE Energy · August 2025 – Present&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Working in 2nd line IT support within a hybrid Azure AD environment. Day-to-day responsibilities span endpoint provisioning via Autopilot and Intune, device lifecycle management for joiners/movers/leavers, and advanced network troubleshooting across VPN, WiFi, and Azure-identity-driven authentication. Also leading documentation and process modernisation projects, using spreadsheet automation and data modelling to standardise and track operational work.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Legal</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/legal/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/legal/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="content"&gt;Content&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;All writing and original images on this site are © Ryan Cranie unless stated otherwise.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="media-data-and-artwork"&gt;Media data and artwork&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Covers and metadata on the &lt;a href="https://www.ryancranie.com/media/"&gt;media&lt;/a&gt; pages come from third-party sources and are hosted on this site. Cover art remains the property of its respective owners.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="tmdb"&gt;TMDB&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.themoviedb.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;img src="https://www.ryancranie.com/img/legal/tmdb.svg" alt="TMDB" width="80" style="display:block;margin:0.5rem 0 0.75rem;"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Film and TV data and images from &lt;a href="https://www.themoviedb.org"&gt;TMDB&lt;/a&gt;. This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Movies</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/movies/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/movies/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Music</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/music/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/music/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Novels</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/novels/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/novels/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Portfolio</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/it-portfolio/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/it-portfolio/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="homelab"&gt;Homelab&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve been running a self-hosted home network - not as a sandbox, but as infrastructure I actually depend on. Everything from DNS and VPN access to media, backups, and game servers runs on it. Designing, breaking, and fixing it has been the most useful technical education I&amp;rsquo;ve had.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The network is segmented into isolated zones: internal services, IoT, home devices, and a public-facing DMZ - enforced by a dedicated firewall with a default-deny policy between segments. The compute layer is a three-node virtualisation cluster. All application deployments are managed through Git and Docker Compose; no click-ops, full rollback capability.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>TV Shows</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/tv/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/tv/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Video Games</title><link>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/games/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.ryancranie.com/media/games/</guid><description/></item></channel></rss>